From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:21:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/43] Let RPC packet helpers execute their guest bodies

The generated packet action test reproduced sceRpcGetFPacket throwing. Remove the three automatic TODO bindings and delete their unused stub files. The disc helpers free packet fields, rotate 64-byte pool slots using signed remainder, and select an indexed pool with rotating fallback; all effects stay in guest registers and memory.

Verified build, quick/full 56 tests, 1106 VU replay runs with zero mismatches/rejections, and boot to title. First-mission reached at 25.2 FPS, CPU user/sys 152.493/2.339 s, zero VU fallbacks and steady audio underruns, no crash or stubs.

